    "gates": "per paid gate (keyed by its name) and config: for each split (dev, train) the bins, lowest score first, or null where the gate judged none of the config's answers on that split, with `empty` giving the reason for each split that has none",
    "bin": "size (answers in the bin), first and last (its lowest and highest gate score), mean_score (the mean gate score, the x), success_rate (the share of the bin's answers that were right, the y), low and high (the percentile 95% interval of the success rate over the paired resamples that draw the bin; null if none does) and undefined (the share of resamples that draw none of the bin's answers)",
    "binning": "about 10 equal-count bins in score order; equal scores are never split across bins (A17 item 21), so heavily tied scores (the Sonnet gate's whole numbers) give fewer and uneven bins",
    "answers": "each paid gate is measured on the answers that pass the free checks; a refused call has no gate score and is left out of the bins"
